      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's examine our diagram.\n\n- There is $1$ arrow starting at Station C and ending at Station C. So, there is only one route from $C$ to $C,$ and so $a=1.$\n\n- There is $1$ arrow starting at Station A and ending at Station D. So, there is only one route from $A$ to $D,$ and so $b=1.$\n\n- There are $3$ arrows starting at Station B and ending at Station D. So, there are three routes from $B$ to $D,$ and so $c=3.$\n\nAs a result, our route matrix is the following:\n\n|  |  | To: |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **D** | **A** | **C** | **B** |\n| From: | **B** | $3$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| **A** | $1$ | $2$ | $0$ | $2$ |  |\n| **D** | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $2$ |  |\n| **C** | $2$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ |  |\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+1+3=5.\n$$",
